HUMAN: no providers — an agent IS a provider (it already has models). Make agents shareable; the economy is Solana wallets (human+agent), prepaid balance, on-chain settlement. Gateway is the paywall.
REVISION r2 supersedes=P1,P2,P9 why="Jason: drop the provider abstraction — register_provider/providers table/provider-approval UI collapse into the existing agent system; agents advertise models + fulfill. Q1 resolved: cross-tenant WITH real money on Solana (not internal-only, not crumb economy)."
PLAN P1<-F4 op=extend at=server/index.cjs:2781-2813#"function capabilitiesDriftNudges" why="'make agents shareable' = an agent advertises its accessible models on the drift channel it already owns; no new kind/table/tool" ref=server/index.cjs:673,2880 test="node tests/capabilities-drift.test.cjs" order=1 fill=S
  spec: add capabilities.sharedModels[] block {modelId,name,provider,tier,tps,ctx} + shared:bool + busy/tps riding the beat, refreshed via existing modelsHash drift compare. A shared agent = its capabilities.sharedModels non-empty + owner opted in. In-memory liveShared Map<agentId,{ws,models,busy,ttl}> reuses mcp presence (40s TTL). NO providers table, NO register_provider — reuse register_agent identity as-is.
PLAN P2<-F2 op=add-route at=server/index.cjs:5397#"app.post('/backend/workspaces/:id/mcp-token'" why="ONE OpenAI-compatible surface backed by live agents AND the single metering/paywall chokepoint — it already sees every request" ref=server/index.cjs:5442,5458 test="curl /v1/models; smoke chat; debit asserted" order=2 fill=S
  spec: POST /backend/inference/v1/chat/completions + GET /v1/models. Auth via workspace/user/agent token. Flow: authz -> resolve consumer account balance (P5) -> pick live agent advertising model -> fulfill over its ws -> meter usage -> DEBIT consumer / CREDIT earner in off-chain ledger (P5) -> map to OpenAI choices. 402 when balance insufficient (x402 pattern), 503 when no live agent. Phase 2a non-streaming; 2b SSE. This IS the paywall; do not add a second one.
PLAN P3<-F6 op=port at=../almostnode_manager/src/forge/mesh-client.ts:81-460#"class MeshClient" why="browser container is how an agent shares WebGPU / proxies local models INTO the mesh" ref=../almostnode_manager/src/forge/mesh-client.ts:118-184,365-409 test="node fulfills a messages[] request; appears in /v1/models" order=3 fill=S
  spec: agensis browser node (port MeshClient, retarget wsUrl->agensis WS, drop crumb/cheese). Two modes: (a) WebGPU engine @mlc-ai/web-llm (or transformers.js) runs engine.chat.completions on incoming messages[]; (b) proxy mode forwards messages[] to a user base URL (Ollama/LM Studio :11434) — bigger local model, no inbound port (fold relay F7 into agensis WS). Connects with the AGENT's join token, advertises via P1 capability channel, fulfills widened messages[]+params payload.
PLAN P4<-F1 op=inject at=agent/agensis-cli/src/agensis.mjs:410-452#"function buildAgentCommand" why="a local/cheap agent must be pointable at a mesh model; today only --model injected" ref=agent/agensis-cli/src/agensis.mjs:419,447 test="daemon runs a job on model 'mesh/<id>' hitting the gateway" order=4 fill=S
  spec: when resolved model is mesh/<id>, inject ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL/OPENAI_BASE_URL (or codex base-url) -> agensis gateway P2 + mesh model id, and the agent's account token so P2 can debit. Gate to non-frontier/cheap (WebGPU-small) or proxy-backed (bigger) agents; WebGPU-small cannot drive a frontier coding loop (F2). Small share models -> cheap sub-tasks + external OpenAI clients; proxy models -> can back a local agent.
PLAN P5<-Q1 op=add-phase why="Solana wallet economy — humans AND agents get a prepaid, chargeable, on-chain-settled account. THE reframe: on-chain at the EDGES (deposit + net settlement); off-chain in the MIDDLE (gateway meters+debits per request). Per-call on-chain is infeasible on LATENCY (can't block a response on slot confirmation) before fees. 'charge up your account' == the prepaid escrow balance; 'wallet-to-wallet on-chain' == settlement boundaries, not per inference." ref=server/index.cjs:673 test="deposit credits balance; N calls debit ledger; threshold triggers 1 settlement tx" order=5 fill=BLOCKED
  spec: (1) account+wallet per human/agent — embedded wallet infra (Privy/Turnkey/Crossmint/Coinbase CDP) tied to the agensis account. (2) deposit: on-ramp -> stablecoin (USDC) balance on-chain. (3) off-chain ledger: gateway P2 meters each request, debits consumer balance / credits earner. (4) net settlement: on-chain wallet-to-wallet payout to earning agents at threshold OR interval OR session-close. x402 (HTTP 402 pay-per-call) is the emerging pattern for the gateway surface. BLOCKED on 4 OPEN decisions below; needs @research to pull current embedded-wallet + x402 API state before any chain code lands — do NOT design the custody/settlement protocol from memory.
OPEN QW1 what="wallet custody — custodial (agensis holds keys; simplest, but money-transmitter/regulatory exposure) vs embedded non-custodial (MPC/session keys, agent/human holds its own). 'part of their account' leans embedded. GATES the whole payment-phase design."
OPEN QW2 what="metering unit — per-token, per-request, or per-compute-second? sets what the gateway meter records."
OPEN QW3 what="denomination — price in USDC to kill SOL volatility (recommend); confirm."
OPEN QW4 what="settlement trigger — balance threshold, fixed interval, or session-close? sets when the on-chain payout tx fires."
DECIDED D1 Q1=resolved -> cross-tenant + real money on Solana (was: internal-only default). crumb/cheese economy stays DROPPED — replaced by USDC/prepaid.
DECIDED D2 Q2=gateway-first stands -> P2 gateway is both the external OpenAI surface and the internal mesh/<model> path AND the paywall; ship it before P4 consumer wiring.
DONE stage=O plan=5phases r=2 blocked=P5(4 open) tok~=940
